SELECT 'kreeghor', 'Kreeghor', 'rifts', '---
id: kreeghor
name: Kreeghor
system: rifts
category: rcc
source_book: Rifts Dimension Book 2: Phase World p.73-74
attribute_dice:
  IQ: "3d6"
  ME: "2d6+12"
  MA: "3d6"
  PS: "3d6+10"
  PP: "3d6+6"
  PE: "4d6"
  PB: "2d4"
  Spd: "4d6"
mdc_base: "2d6x10+20, plus 3d6 per level of experience"
ppe_base: "3d6+6"
psionics_allowed: false
bonuses:
  combat: { initiative: 2, strike: 1, parry: 1, dodge: 1 }
  saves: { spell_magic: 2, psionics: 2 }
natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Supernatural Strength and Endurance", description: "P.S. and P.E. are both SUPERNATURAL. The kreeghor were bio-engineered as warrior slaves by the Splugorth and are built for nothing else." }
  - { name: "Claws and Bite", description: "Claws add 2D6 M.D. to hand to hand damage; the bite inflicts 2D6 M.D." }
  - { name: "Enhanced Reflexes and Speed", description: "The source of the +2 initiative and the +1 to strike, parry and dodge carried in the class bonuses." }
  - { name: "Bio-Regeneration", description: "1D6 M.D.C. per hour." }
  - { name: "Resistant to Psionics", description: "A kreeghor cannot use psionics at all, and saves against them at +2." }
  - { name: "Horror Factor", description: "9. A number the kreeghor projects, which the sheet has no field for." }
  - { name: "Average Life Span", description: "120 years." }
  - { name: "Size", description: "Six to eight feet (1.8 to 2.4 m) fully erect, though they habitually stand crouched; 180 to 250 lbs (82 to 113 kg)." }
side_effects: "DOUBLE DAMAGE FROM MAGIC. Magic attacks and magic weapons - techno-wizard, rune and holy weapons included - inflict twice normal damage on a kreeghor. It is believed to be Splugorth meddling, built in deliberately to make the race easier to control."
extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified against a 200 dpi render of
    printed 74, which carries the whole stat block. The lore runs from printed
    73 and both pages were read to the end.
  - A RACE CARRIES NO xp_table. Printed 183 heads the relevant column "Seljuk,
    Noro Mystic Warrior, Kreeghor, and Catyr", which this race shares with three
    others - but composition is race-primary, so a table here would win over the
    occupation''s and silently drop it. The ladder is: 0, 2,201, 4,401, 8,901,
    18,001, 26,001, 36,001, 52,001, 76,001, 100,001, 150,001, 200,001, 275,001,
    350,001, 425,001. It is the same ladder the catyr and the seljuk carry, and
    both of those record it here for the same reason.
  - CANNOT DEVELOP PSIONICS, stated outright: "Psionic Powers: None. Kreeghor
    are resistant to psionics, but cannot use them." That is
    `psionics_allowed: false`, which is modelled - `rollsForPsionics()` reads it
    and the wizard''s Race briefing shows it - and is not the same as simply
    having no psionics block, which would let the character roll on the Random
    Psionics Table. The resistance itself is the +2 save in `bonuses`.
  - THE DOUBLE DAMAGE FROM MAGIC IS DISPLAY ONLY. `side_effects` is prose the
    sheet shows and nothing computes; the app has no damage-taken model to apply
    a multiplier to. It is the most important number on this race''s page and a
    GM has to apply it by hand.
  - MAGIC POWERS: NONE, and it is a statement about study rather than a
    restriction - "They never study magic, although they may use magic weapons
    and items." Unlike the seljuk, whose whole race spent its P.P.E., a kreeghor
    has 3D6+6 P.P.E. and simply does not learn. No `occ_restrictions` is
    written; it is in the GM Notes.
  - A natural M.D.C. creature, so `mdc_base` carries the roll and there is no
    S.D.C. and no CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS entry.
  - The race states no Money, no Cybernetics and NO SKILLS AT ALL - no R.C.C.
    skill list, no related and no secondary. That is correct rather than
    missing: everything a kreeghor knows comes from its O.C.C.
  - The book prints "Available as an optional player character" above the stat
    block, which is its own sanction. The Royal Kreeghor on the facing page is
    labelled "NPC Villains" and is NOT imported.
---

## Lore

A kreeghor is a vaguely humanoid thing with long arms and legs ending in sharp
claws, standing in a permanent crouch as though about to leap. A spiny ridge
runs down the head and back. The crocodile hide is brown-green, blue-green or
mottled black on dark green, and the eyes are large red or white orbs. Males and
females are almost indistinguishable, the same size and equally deadly.

They are a warrior race with a ten-thousand-year tradition of conquest, which
they uphold to this day. Some scholars have argued that instincts that savage
should have stopped them cooperating well enough to build an advanced
civilization - and they were probably right, because the kreeghor did not build
it. The Splugorth gave it to them.

## The only species that ever got out

The Splugorth found a savage race and decided it would make ideal warriors. They
handed over advanced tools and machines, added some bio-wizard enhancements, and
trained the kreeghor as warrior slaves. Once the kreeghor could use the
machines, and had built a social structure that held together, they revolted.

They were led by a mysterious group of super-kreeghor whose origins are still
argued over - the Gene-Splicers, bio-wizard modification, or the Cosmic Forge,
which is naturally the version the kreeghor promote. The Royal Kreeghor were few
but faster, stronger and tougher than the rest, and even Splugorth Conservators
found themselves outmatched.

Under them the kreeghor slaughtered the Kittani and Kydian advisors who had
trained them, and blew up the Splugorth intelligence in charge of their planet.
They had apparently been stockpiling weapons for decades. After a twenty-year
war the Splugorth gave up trying to retake them and withdrew from that part of
the Three Galaxies - but not before blocking every transdimensional gateway to
and from the planet.

The kreeghor are the only known species ever to break free of Splugorth control
and live to tell it. The Splugorth put it down to the incompetence of the lord
who died at the rebels'' hands. Others suspect a renegade Splugorth lord, or a
hostile god or intelligence, engineered the whole thing.

## The Transgalactic Empire

They conquered several dozen planets, absorbed many alien races, and founded the
Transgalactic Empire, which they intend to keep. Most kreeghor consider
themselves the epitome of evolution and are certain they are fated to rule the
Three Galaxies - and after that, the Emperor muses, the Megaverse.

Non-warrior kreeghor exist and are held in contempt by their peers. The typical
kreeghor scientist specializes in military applications, as do most of its
technicians, artists and craftsmen.

## GM Notes

A few kreeghor become renegades and leave the Empire. Some are criminals brutal
enough to offend even their own race. Others have grown disgusted with the
Empire''s policies and work against it, and some have simply forsaken the warrior
ways for a quieter life. Any of them can be a player character with the Game
Master''s sanction, and the book says so - but expect fellow kreeghor to read the
character as a misanthrope, a traitor or a coward, and rebels and free men to
read them as a spy, a brigand or a monster.

Kreeghor go into men-at-arms O.C.C.s, mercenaries and wilderness scouts
included, and above all the Imperial Legionnaire. They never study magic, though
they will happily use a magic weapon.

The thing that kills a kreeghor is magic. Every magic attack and magic weapon,
techno-wizard, rune and holy items included, does double damage to one. Nothing
on the character sheet applies that; it is on the GM.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kreeghor');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'kreeghor';

